<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 77,353 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 77,353 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 77,353 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 46,006 tonnes in the same period on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Sunday	September 14</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   1,625	7,527</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  75,728     38,479</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, five were expected to sail and six were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>The port observed a public holiday on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  74,000	 Chesa Peak City    16/9</p>
<p>Container		   558	 CMB Melody	   16/9</p>
<p>Container		   309	 Ocean Strength     16/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
